@startuml sequence_communication
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam maxMessageSize 250

title Service Communication Flow\n(gRPC over HTTP/2 + Consul service discovery)

participant "Client\n(FastAPI bridge,\npeer service,\nor Robot Framework)" as Client
participant "Consul agent" as Consul
participant "Service A\n(ServiceRunner)" as Service

== Phase 1: Service Registration ==

note over Service
  On startup, ServiceRunner reads
  Settings (env-driven), wires up
  the gRPC server, then registers
  itself with the local Consul agent.
end note

Service -> Service : ServiceRunner::run()\n  bind gRPC port\n  start grpc::Server\n  enable reflection
Service -> Consul : PUT /v1/agent/service/register\n{ id, name, address, port,\n  check: {grpc, interval=3s} }
note over Consul #fff3e0
  Consul catalog now lists service A
  with a healthy gRPC TCP check.
end note

== Phase 2: Discovery (Consul) ==

note over Client
  Whoever wants to call service A
  asks Consul where it lives.  No
  pre-shared host:port, no broker.
end note

Client -> Consul : GET /v1/health/service/<name>?passing
Consul --> Client : [ { Service: { Address, Port } } ]

note over Client
  Client now has the address:port
  for one (or more) healthy
  instances of service A.
end note

== Phase 3: gRPC call ==

Client -> Service : grpc::Channel(address:port)\nServiceStub::Method(req) over HTTP/2
note over Service
  No correlation_id, no reply queue.
  HTTP/2 streams + protobuf framing
  match request to response natively.
end note
Service -> Service : adapter dispatches to domain\nbuild Response message
Service --> Client : Method response\n(unary or stream)

== Phase 4: Method discovery (optional, via reflection) ==

note over Client
  Manager GUI / grpcurl can list
  methods at runtime without a
  pre-shared .proto file.
end note

Client -> Service : grpc.reflection.v1alpha\n  ServerReflection.ServerReflectionInfo
Service --> Client : file descriptors\n(services + methods + message types)

== Phase 5: Shutdown ==

note over Service
  On SIGTERM / SIGBREAK, ServiceRunner
  drains in-flight RPCs and tells
  Consul to forget the instance.
end note

Service -> Service : Server::Shutdown(deadline)
Service -> Consul : PUT /v1/agent/service/deregister/<id>
Consul -> Consul : drop instance from catalog\n(any client doing the\nPhase 2 lookup now skips it)

== What replaced the broker ==

note over Client, Service
  **No exchange / queue / routing key.**
  | **Was (RabbitMQ era)** | **Is (gRPC era)** |
  | services_request exchange | direct gRPC channel client→server |
  | service_information topic | Consul catalog (HTTP API + TTL) |
  | services_update fanout | Consul long-poll / GUI 1s refresh |
  | reply_to + correlation_id | HTTP/2 stream framing |
  | svc_api_* prefix | proto package.Service/Method |
end note

@enduml
